{"name":"Jute","hex":"#ad9773","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Jute","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A member of the Germanic tribe that existed in modern-day Denmark that invaded England about the same time as the Angles and the Saxons in the beginning of the Middle Ages, but were eventually integrated by the time of the Norman Conquest."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Jute"}],"entries":[{"title":"Jute","blocks":[{"text":"Jute is a long, rough, shiny bast fibre that can be spun into coarse, strong threads. It is produced from flowering plants in the genus Corchorus, of the mallow family Malvaceae. The primary source of the fiber is Corchorus olitorius, but such fiber is considered inferior to that derived from Corchorus capsularis."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Jute_-_Kolkata_2003-10-31_00538.JPG/330px-Jute_-_Kolkata_2003-10-31_00538.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jute","wikidata":"Q107211"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Jute_Field_Bangladesh_%287749587518%29.jpg/500px-Jute_Field_Bangladesh_%287749587518%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Jute_Field_Bangladesh_%287749587518%29.jpg/500px-Jute_Field_Bangladesh_%287749587518%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A jute field in Bangladesh","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJute_Field_Bangladesh_(7749587518).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Jute_Rope_%28%E0%AE%9A%E0%AE%A3%E0%AE%B2%E0%AF%8D_%E0%AE%95%E0%AE%AF%E0%AE%BF%E0%AE%B1%E0%AF%81%29.jpg/500px-Jute_Rope_%28%E0%AE%9A%E0%AE%A3%E0%AE%B2%E0%AF%8D_%E0%AE%95%E0%AE%AF%E0%AE%BF%E0%AE%B1%E0%AF%81%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parse